# This directory is deliberately empty.
#
# Vercel finishes a build and then refuses to deploy unless a static output
# directory exists: `No Output Directory named "public" found after the Build
# completed`. This backend has no static output — it is one serverless function
# (`api/index.js`) behind a catch-all rewrite — so it needs a directory that
# exists and contains nothing.
#
# Pointing `outputDirectory` at `dist/` instead would satisfy the same check and
# be worse: `dist/` is the compiled server (plus `.js.map` source maps, which
# embed the original TypeScript), and Vercel serves static files *before*
# applying rewrites, so `/routes/items.js` and `/app.js.map` would be publicly
# downloadable. An empty directory publishes nothing while still passing the
# check.
